On Saturday, January 10, 2015 at 4:04:18 PM UTC-5, Joshua Pritikin wrote:
> Gosh, I can't wait to use 'auto' type declarations, but are CRAN
> packages allowed to use C++11 features? My impression was that the CRAN
> team was moving extremely slowly on C++ compiler requirements and wanted
> to maintain compatibility with ancient versions of C++ for as long as
> possible (or longer). Am I misinformed?

It is allowed now

http://cran.r-project.org/doc/manuals/r-release/R-exts.html#Using-C_002b_002b11-code

but is limited by only having a port of g++-4.6 available for Windows, which does support auto but not much else from the C++11 standard.

Avi is involved in trying to upgrade the toolchain for the next R release. See this thread:

https://stat.ethz.ch/pipermail/r-devel/2015-January/070355.html

Duncan subsequently said "maybe".

Ben

