From u6db62e08ec862130 at groups.google.com  Thu Jan 22 13:35:51 2015
From: u6db62e08ec862130 at groups.google.com (Joshua N Pritikin)
Date: Thu, 22 Jan 2015 13:35:51 +0000
Subject: 2 kinds of error checking
Message-ID: <qeR99Io4_gE.KudJZ6a7Us8J@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-dev/c/qeR99Io4_gE/m/KudJZ6a7Us8J>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I find with a perusal of the source code that there are two kinds of
error checks.

+ Checks that only need to be done once to verify that the model can be
evaluated (like matrix conformability checking).

+ Checks that need to be done at every iteration (like checking whether
a covariance matrix is positive definite).

Currently, it appears that both of these types of checks are done at
every iteration. Do we have a plan to split up these checks into
separate parts of the generated source code?

--
Joshua N. Pritikin
Department of Psychology
University of Virginia
485 McCormick Rd, Gilmer Hall Room 102
Charlottesville, VA 22904
http://people.virginia.edu/~jnp3bc

