So, after finding the slow-down, I took a couple days to add a test that runs a simple model 100 times and records the output. Each run is about 3 seconds, so it takes 5 minutes to run.

I ran it on the Jenkins machine over each of the merge commits since v2.5.0 (including v2.5.0).

I've plotted the time range in gray, added 50% intervals in black, and the average as a circle. I'm going to create a pull request to add this test into our development branch and I'll create a new job for Jenkins to run every pull request and every merge. I don't know how to have a running plot in Jenkins, but we'll figure it out.

I've also attached the raw data in case you wanted to see it. If you think it should be doing something else, please let me know.

Daniel

